Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: supermox-dhcp-client
Architecture: all
Depends: pve-container,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: thin alias for SuperMox's one DHCP path (transitional)
  crhy/SuperMox#9 landed two answers to the missing isc-dhcp-client at once:
  this package's /usr/sbin/dhclient adapter (f079) and pve-container's
  0003-maintained-dhcp-client patch (f099). The patch won: for a
  host-managed container NIC the patched PVE::LXC::manage_dhclient probes
  the container image itself (dhclient, udhcpc6 or udhcpc) and runs that
  client through the /usr/share/lxc/hooks/pve-dhcp-client adapter that
  pve-container now ships, so the job needs no host binary at all.
  This package therefore ships no files any more: no /usr/sbin/dhclient,
  and no Provides/Replaces/Conflicts on isc-dhcp-client, so the interim
  isc-dhcp fork stands as the only package that can own /usr/sbin/dhclient
  (dropping that fork is rhY's decision, not this package's). It stays as
  a thin alias that pulls in pve-container, which carries the adapter and
  depends on the maintained client (udhcpc | dhcpcd-base), so anything
  still referencing supermox-dhcp-client keeps working on one path.
